## The top station

::bg{location="funicular_top" time="morning"}
::music{action="start" mood="peaceful" volume="down"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: The funicular car shudders the last ten metres and stops against the buffers with a sound like a dropped drawer.
@narrator{code="0020"}: Hallen Ridge Weather Station: two stone huts, a mast, a white louvred box on legs, and more sky than you have ever been under.
@narrator{code="0030" when="has(prev.run.route)"}: It looks exactly as you left it last summer. The door still sticks.

::use{component="enter" who="ines" instance="use-001"}
@ines{code="0010" emotion="stern"}: You're the intern. You're early. Good.
@ines{code="0020" emotion="neutral"}: Ines Halvorsen. I run this place, which mostly means I write down what the sky did and apologise to it.
@player{code="0010"}: The brochure said "a quiet summer of observation."
@ines{code="0030" emotion="happy"}: The brochure is also forty years old.

## The job

::bg{location="deck" time="morning"}
::use{component="enter" who="ines" side="left" instance="use-002"}
@ines{code="0040"}: Readings at seven, one, and seven. Temperature, humidity, pressure, wind, cloud. You write them in the log and you do not round.
@ines{code="0050"}: Sol keeps the radio. Nights, mostly. You'll meet him or you won't; he's a rumour until noon.
@ines{code="0060" emotion="worried"}: And the village wants something from us this year.

<branch id="village" prompt="Ines taps a letter pinned by the barometer.">
  <choice id="ask" label="Ask what the village wants">
    @ines{code="0070"}: The Lantern Festival is Sunday night. Maren wants a forecast by Friday, so they know whether to hang the lanterns or cancel.
    @ines{code="0080" emotion="stern"}: A real forecast. Signed. That means you and I, with a week of your readings.
    ::accept{quest="forecast"}
  </choice>
  <choice id="shrug" label="Say you're only here for the readings">
    @ines{code="0090" emotion="neutral"}: That's the job. The forecast is mine, then.
    @ines{code="0100"}: If you change your mind, it's due Friday. The village doesn't forgive a wet festival.
    ::accept{quest="forecast"}
  </choice>
</branch>

@ines{code="0110"}: Go and look around. The station is small. You'll run out of it by lunch.
::auto{character="ines" action="fadeOut"}
